    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d417-f1" n="2" xml:id="d417-f1-content">
                <p>In Matthews’ copy of the Briefing Book,
                    this supplement has been thoroughly revised (see <ref target="#d327-f18"
                        >document No. 327, footnotes 26</ref> and <ref target="#d327-f1">29</ref>).
                    The pertinent passages of the revision are as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“14. During the period of occupation Germany shall be treated as a single
                            economic unit. To this end: <list>
                                <item>“(i) no barriers should be erected to the movement of goods
                                    and services which are required for (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                        >a</hi>) the discharge of Germany’s reparation obligations,
                                        (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the maintenance of
                                    occupying forces and displaced persons, and (<hi
                                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) the maintenance of a subsistence
                                    standard of living in Germany.</item>
                                <item>
                                    <p>“(ii) To the fullest extent possible there shall be Uniform
                                        Ration Scales throughout Germany[.]</p>
                                    <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                                </item>
                                <item>“(v) There shall be Agreed Programs on German Coal Production
                                    and Allocation[.]”</item>
                            </list>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
